ROLLBACK;
-- a merge stopped and kept (dolt.allow_commit_conflicts): durable, shown
-- to other sessions, and a commit refused until it is resolved; an abort
-- clears it.  Without the setting, outside a transaction block, the merge
-- is rolled back.
SELECT dolt_merge('keeps_old');
ERROR:  merge conflict detected, transaction rolled back
DETAIL:  Table ic.t is another table on the other side, a relation of its own of that name: a table identity conflict.
HINT:  Merge in a transaction block to resolve it with dolt_conflicts_resolve('--ours') or ('--theirs') before committing, or set dolt.allow_commit_conflicts to keep it.
SET dolt.allow_commit_conflicts = on;
SELECT (dolt_merge('keeps_old'))[2:4] AS merged;
         merged          
-------------------------
 {0,1,"conflicts found"}
(1 row)

RESET dolt.allow_commit_conflicts;
